      "worked": "Complete the square:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=x^2+4x+4+5\\\\y&=(x+2)^2+5.\\end{align*}$$\nThe vertex is $(-2,5)$ and the axis of symmetry is $x=-2$. Since $a=1>0$, the parabola is concave up.\n\nAt $x=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=0^2+4(0)+9\\\\y&=9.\\end{align*}$$\nThe $y$-intercept is $(0,9)$.\n\nSince $(x+2)^2\\ge0$, we have $y\\ge5>0$. There are no real $x$-intercepts. The sketch lies entirely above the $x$-axis.",
